 "chapter": "Five days ago",
 "topic": "What if GTA6 cheat codes worked in real life?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "You fall down all fourteen stairs. You land on your head. And you stand up without a scratch."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "You open your sock drawer, and there's a quarter of a million dollars in it. Again."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "You press five buttons, and a bright red sports car drops out of the sky onto your driveway."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "And this morning, you flew to school. Over the traffic. With a jetpack."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "Five days ago, you bought an old game controller at a yard sale for two dollars. Taped to the back was a list. Twelve cheat codes. And one more line at the bottom, scratched out so hard the pen went through the paper."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "So what if video game cheat codes worked in real life? Not in a game. In your street. On your body. In your bank."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p7",
   "text": "And what if every single one of them came with a catch?"
  }
